WEBVTT

00:01.314 --> 00:03.650
MARCH 16, 2006

00:05.109 --> 00:07.487
Chifuyu, I need to Time Leap.

00:07.570 --> 00:08.655
Huh?

00:09.447 --> 00:10.823
I see.

00:11.407 --> 00:13.743
Finally going back 12 years in the future.

00:14.452 --> 00:15.703
Gonna miss you, partner.

00:16.329 --> 00:19.499
It's not that.
I only want to go back a couple of days.

00:19.582 --> 00:20.750
Huh?

00:20.833 --> 00:22.835
It was White Day two days ago!

00:22.919 --> 00:26.714
I was supposed to give Hina her present,
but I totally spaced out and forgot.

00:26.798 --> 00:28.591
<i>She's gonna kill me!</i>

00:28.675 --> 00:29.676
RUMBLE RUMBLE

00:29.759 --> 00:33.888
What do I do, Chifuyu? How do I face Hina?
I'm so screwed!

00:33.972 --> 00:36.766
Put your hands back on the handle bars,
you idiot!

00:36.849 --> 00:38.393
- [crashing]
- [grunting]

00:41.729 --> 00:44.023
Sorry, about that, Chifuyu.

00:44.107 --> 00:45.108
Takemitchy.

00:45.191 --> 00:46.276
Huh?

00:46.359 --> 00:48.361
Even though we missed the actual day,

00:48.444 --> 00:50.488
I think there's a way
that you can save it.

00:50.572 --> 00:51.572
Huh?

00:51.656 --> 00:53.074
It's foolproof.

00:53.157 --> 00:55.118
The Great T2D2 Plan!

00:55.618 --> 00:59.914
"T2D2"?
What is that? Some type of code word?

00:59.998 --> 01:01.499
Let me break it down for you.

01:01.582 --> 01:04.419
It stands for Time Travel and Doki Doki.

01:04.502 --> 01:05.503
THE GREAT TIME TRAVEL DOKI DOKI
T2D2 PLAN.

01:05.587 --> 01:06.963
'Cause it'll make her heart race!

01:08.339 --> 01:09.424
Yeah?

01:10.925 --> 01:12.969
[♪ theme song playing]

02:40.640 --> 02:41.808
[Takemichi] What are these?

02:42.392 --> 02:44.894
- They're love's secret weapon.
- Huh?

02:44.977 --> 02:48.189
The plan is to use these boxes
to set up a dramatic surprise,

02:48.272 --> 02:50.775
to reveal the White Day gift
you forgot to give Hina.

02:50.858 --> 02:53.736
She's going to feel like
the luckiest girl in the world.

02:53.820 --> 02:56.823
That's exactly what I want.
I still don't get it though.

02:56.906 --> 03:00.326
All I see are polka dot boxes,
ribbons and a notebook.

03:00.410 --> 03:04.539
[laughs] Takemitchy,
girls can't resist these things.

03:04.622 --> 03:08.334
Cute little ribbons, polka dot boxes
and big surprises.

03:09.043 --> 03:10.378
I read it in a manga once.

03:10.461 --> 03:13.005
Whoa! I had no idea you were an expert.

03:13.089 --> 03:13.965
MARCH 16

03:14.048 --> 03:17.301
[Chifuyu] The first step is to write dates
on the boxes starting from two days ago.

03:17.385 --> 03:20.763
When she opens them,
you'll also give Hina a note with a clue.

03:21.556 --> 03:25.226
First clue: "You go up me with your feet,
and down me on your butt.

03:25.309 --> 03:26.894
Can you figure out what I am?"

03:27.854 --> 03:28.855
It's a slide, isn't it?

03:28.938 --> 03:31.566
That's correct!
Is your name Einstein or something?

03:31.649 --> 03:34.735
So, when Hina walks over to the slide...

03:34.819 --> 03:35.862
ta-da!

03:35.945 --> 03:38.614
She'll see another box
with March 16th written on it,

03:38.698 --> 03:40.491
which will contain the second clue.

03:40.575 --> 03:41.576
Let's see.

03:41.659 --> 03:45.872
"No matter how long you ride me,
you'll still be stuck in the same place."

03:46.789 --> 03:48.374
Hmm...

03:48.458 --> 03:49.459
The answer's a swing!

03:49.542 --> 03:51.669
Bingo! You're a genius!

03:51.752 --> 03:54.839
So when Hina walks over
to check the swing, what will she see?

03:55.465 --> 03:58.426
The next box with March 15th on it!

03:58.509 --> 04:01.095
Wow! This is amazing, Chifuyu!

04:01.179 --> 04:03.347
It'll be like
we're actually time traveling!

04:03.431 --> 04:05.808
[chuckles]
Ready for the grand finale, Takemitchy.

04:07.351 --> 04:08.352
[grunts]

04:08.436 --> 04:10.396
[Takemichi]
"You won't get hurt if you fall in me,

04:10.480 --> 04:14.317
but you can use what I have inside
to blind someone. What am I?"

04:14.400 --> 04:15.902
Hmm...

04:19.113 --> 04:20.198
Come on.

04:20.281 --> 04:21.491
This is the easiest one.

04:21.574 --> 04:23.201
- There's nothing that I can--
- [footsteps running]

04:23.284 --> 04:24.911
[shouting]

04:24.994 --> 04:26.162
[grunting]

04:26.245 --> 04:29.457
If you wanna win Hina's heart,
you're gonna have to try harder than that!

04:32.835 --> 04:35.046
- It's the sandbox!
- Exactly!

04:35.129 --> 04:38.466
She'll open the last box and be surprised
with your White Day present

04:38.549 --> 04:40.426
and a final message inside that says,

04:40.510 --> 04:43.012
"There was no other day
I could've given this to you"!

04:43.095 --> 04:45.139
You're just like Socrates!

04:45.223 --> 04:48.059
I'm so lucky
that you're my friend, Chifuyu!

04:48.142 --> 04:51.020
- This'll turn everything around!
- Yeah!

04:52.313 --> 04:54.357
Now all I have to do is add the present.

04:55.525 --> 04:58.027
- A ring, huh?
- Yep.

04:58.110 --> 05:00.488
I really hope that Hina likes the design.

05:00.571 --> 05:03.115
Of course she will.
She's gonna love the surprise too.

05:03.199 --> 05:05.326
I think we're ready to start the plan.

05:05.409 --> 05:06.786
Got it!

05:12.291 --> 05:14.544
[gasps] It's game time, Takemitchy.

05:17.630 --> 05:18.631
Hina.

05:23.219 --> 05:24.512
Hey, Takemichi.

05:24.595 --> 05:30.726
<i>Okay, so, maybe I should apologize first,
and then I'll give her the letter?</i>

05:30.810 --> 05:34.647
<i>Crap! I feel like I can't breathe.</i>

05:36.691 --> 05:38.818
- [Hina] I'm sorry.
- Huh?

05:39.318 --> 05:40.444
Why?

05:40.528 --> 05:42.905
Sorry I haven't really been myself.

05:43.990 --> 05:47.743
Between the two of us,
you're probably hurting more than I am.

05:47.827 --> 05:50.204
Huh?
I wish I could hear what they're saying.

05:50.830 --> 05:52.915
Why is Hina bowing like that?

05:53.499 --> 05:57.336
After what happened that day,
I feel like I haven't been the same.

05:59.213 --> 06:02.592
Ever since I saw Kisaki die
right in front of me...

06:04.510 --> 06:06.053
I can still see him.

06:06.137 --> 06:08.598
I keep replaying what happened...

06:09.891 --> 06:11.267
and I'm so scared.

06:12.101 --> 06:13.853
[sobbing]

06:13.936 --> 06:17.231
I can't stop thinking about how Kisaki
and Emma are gone.

06:17.315 --> 06:21.193
What if it was my fault
that they both died?

06:22.236 --> 06:23.404
Hina...

06:24.488 --> 06:26.908
<i>I had no idea what you were going through.</i>

06:26.991 --> 06:28.117
[growls]

06:28.200 --> 06:30.578
What are you saying to her, Takemitchy?

06:30.661 --> 06:32.079
Just stick to the script.

06:32.163 --> 06:34.707
The Great T2D2 Plan is a guarantee.

06:34.790 --> 06:36.042
Have her look under the slide.

06:36.125 --> 06:37.543
[crying]

06:39.086 --> 06:40.254
Hina.

06:43.507 --> 06:45.885
You idiot! The sandbox is the finale!

06:46.886 --> 06:48.930
Hina, here.

06:51.182 --> 06:52.308
A ring?

06:52.391 --> 06:53.601
Yeah.

06:53.684 --> 06:56.646
For White Day. Sorry your gift is late.

06:58.189 --> 07:00.316
What the hell is happening?

07:00.399 --> 07:03.527
Listen, I know I don't have
any special skills,

07:04.695 --> 07:06.614
and I'll probably never get rich.

07:08.741 --> 07:09.950
But I promise...

07:10.034 --> 07:12.995
that taking care of you
and making you happy

07:13.079 --> 07:14.914
will always be my priority.

07:18.542 --> 07:19.752
Hina...

07:20.544 --> 07:22.213
will you please marry me?

07:22.296 --> 07:23.714
[gasps]

07:23.798 --> 07:26.592
- Marry?
- Whenever life gets scary,

07:26.676 --> 07:29.011
I'll be right here to protect you
and keep you safe.

07:30.179 --> 07:33.224
I'm here for you, so please don't cry.

07:33.307 --> 07:35.017
[whimpering]

07:36.519 --> 07:37.895
[clears throat]

07:38.938 --> 07:41.857
Twelve years from now, let's get married.

07:42.733 --> 07:44.527
You two are going to get married?

07:44.610 --> 07:47.988
Quiet down, Naoto!
Do you want the entire world to know?

07:48.072 --> 07:50.324
We're going to wait until we're adults,
of course.

07:50.408 --> 07:52.743
Talk about a spontaneous proposal.

07:52.827 --> 07:55.371
Even my heart's going "doki doki" now.

07:55.454 --> 07:57.998
Thanks for coming here
so last-minute, Naoto.

07:59.333 --> 08:02.002
This is the same park
where we had our first handshake.

08:03.212 --> 08:06.048
It feels right
to have our last one in this place too.

08:06.674 --> 08:08.467
Thank you for everything, Naoto.

08:09.093 --> 08:11.470
I couldn't have done
any of this without you.

08:11.554 --> 08:15.057
I'm only here now because you
and your future self had faith in me.

08:15.141 --> 08:17.852
[gasps] So, does that mean in the future,

08:17.935 --> 08:19.895
that my sister and I were saved?

08:19.979 --> 08:21.480
Yes. Definitely.

08:22.857 --> 08:24.984
It's time. Shake my hand.

08:30.698 --> 08:32.616
Chifuyu. Hina.

08:33.993 --> 08:35.369
See you in the future.

08:38.914 --> 08:40.291
[gasps]

08:42.793 --> 08:44.211
I'm back to the future.

08:45.379 --> 08:46.839
<i>That must mean</i>

08:46.922 --> 08:48.424
<i>that everything worked out!</i>

08:48.507 --> 08:50.301
<i>Naoto must be alive!</i>

08:51.427 --> 08:54.346
<i>Wait a minute.
Why am I in a tux right now?</i>

08:54.972 --> 08:56.807
<i>And where exactly am I?</i>

08:56.891 --> 08:58.350
[tolling]

08:58.434 --> 09:00.394
<i>A tuxedo and bells ringing...</i>

09:01.103 --> 09:02.980
<i>Huh? Could it be...</i>

09:03.064 --> 09:04.690
<i>Let's get married.</i>

09:04.774 --> 09:06.776
[gasps] <i>No way!</i>

09:11.072 --> 09:12.448
[Hina] There you are!

09:13.032 --> 09:14.909
We're going to be late to the reception!

09:15.868 --> 09:16.869
Hina...

09:18.412 --> 09:22.416
<i>After all this time,
it's finally happening.</i>

09:24.877 --> 09:27.630
You can't keep
the man of the hour waiting. Come on!

09:27.713 --> 09:29.298
Who are we talking about?

09:29.381 --> 09:31.675
It's Hayashida's wedding today, remember?

09:31.759 --> 09:33.511
<i>Wait, who's Hayashida?</i>

09:33.594 --> 09:35.012
We need to hurry up!

09:35.096 --> 09:38.974
<i>Hold on! My brain needs to catch up!
My head's about to explode!</i>

09:43.020 --> 09:44.730
[Ken] You're late, Takemitchy.

09:44.814 --> 09:46.899
- Huh?
- Hurry up and sit down.

09:46.982 --> 09:51.237
[MC] And now, the couple of the hour,
please give it up for the bride and groom!

09:51.320 --> 09:52.321
[applause]

09:53.989 --> 09:57.368
So, Hayashida is Pah-chin?

09:57.451 --> 10:01.831
Uh, thank you for joining us.
It's a beautiful day today

10:01.914 --> 10:05.334
with sunny skies and not
a single cloud in sight, and, yeah...

10:05.417 --> 10:06.794
Is this a weather forecast?

10:06.877 --> 10:10.131
You asshole! Don't you know
Pah-chin barely has two brain cells?

10:10.214 --> 10:11.382
He's doing his best!

10:11.465 --> 10:13.551
Peh-yan has always had a way with words.

10:13.634 --> 10:16.595
- [Ryohei] Shut up, Mitsuya!
- Calm down and give it a rest, Peh-yan.

10:16.679 --> 10:20.015
I'm gonna kill all of you
if you guys keep being so loud!

10:20.099 --> 10:21.559
Says the one yelling right now.

10:21.642 --> 10:24.311
Oh, man, Pah-chin's speech
is all over the place.

10:24.395 --> 10:28.274
I guess some things never change.
Right? Takemitchy.

10:28.357 --> 10:30.359
[Pah-chin] The two of us always...

10:30.442 --> 10:32.945
What's up? Are you about to cry?

10:33.028 --> 10:35.406
We're supposed to be happy, Takemichi.

10:36.073 --> 10:38.784
<i>I can't believe that everyone's alive.</i>

10:39.451 --> 10:41.328
<i>Everyone looks so happy.</i>

10:41.996 --> 10:43.706
<i>Smiling and laughing together.</i>

10:45.207 --> 10:46.292
Is everything okay?

10:47.418 --> 10:48.878
Yes, just...

10:48.961 --> 10:50.504
I can't believe we did it.

10:52.047 --> 10:53.215
<i>I'll never forget that day...</i>

10:53.966 --> 10:57.386
Until I can reach the future
where you're finally safe,

10:57.469 --> 10:58.971
I'm never going to quit trying!

10:59.555 --> 11:00.556
<i>I made a promise.</i>

11:02.391 --> 11:03.684
<i>And now you're here...</i>

11:05.060 --> 11:06.312
<i>right in front of me.</i>

11:07.271 --> 11:08.939
[Ryohei] Pretend like it's an enemy.

11:09.023 --> 11:12.109
- Do it in one clean cut.
- Show us how it's done, Pah-chin.

11:12.193 --> 11:13.819
It should be a piece of cake for you.

11:13.903 --> 11:15.279
- Slice it!
- Hurry up!

11:15.362 --> 11:16.614
- Come on!
- We're waiting.

11:16.697 --> 11:18.866
- Do it.
- Shut the hell up!

11:18.949 --> 11:21.327
- [all laughing]
- It's hard to believe, Takemichi.

11:21.410 --> 11:22.494
Huh?

11:22.578 --> 11:26.081
It was 12 years ago today
that you came back here, isn't it?

11:29.001 --> 11:30.419
When I think about it...

11:31.045 --> 11:35.633
it's crazy that the age you were back then
is the exact same age I am right now.

11:37.676 --> 11:42.181
I have been waiting so long
for this day to finally come.

11:42.264 --> 11:43.432
[applauding]

11:43.515 --> 11:45.601
Welcome home, Takemichi.

11:47.645 --> 11:49.605
This isn't a dream, is it, Hina?

11:49.688 --> 11:51.357
Do you want me to pinch you?

11:51.440 --> 11:52.816
[weeping]

11:53.776 --> 11:55.778
I'm not the only one
who's been waiting for you.

11:56.403 --> 11:58.155
It's kind of funny, isn't it?

11:58.239 --> 11:59.740
For us, it's been 12 whole years.

11:59.823 --> 12:03.619
But for you, Takemichi,
we only just said goodbye, didn't we?

12:04.161 --> 12:06.080
You just proposed to Hina at the park too.

12:06.705 --> 12:08.540
That's pretty wild to think about.

12:08.624 --> 12:11.293
I mean, the reason
we're all even alive right now

12:11.377 --> 12:13.379
is because of what you did, Takemitchy.

12:13.462 --> 12:14.755
Chifuyu...

12:15.297 --> 12:16.715
and Draken...

12:16.799 --> 12:19.301
- So thank you for everything.
- So wanna say thanks for everything.

12:20.803 --> 12:22.554
You're incredible, you know that?

12:23.222 --> 12:25.808
Countless lives were saved
because you never gave up.

12:27.101 --> 12:29.395
I couldn't have done it without you guys.

12:29.478 --> 12:31.647
All of you helped me along the way.

12:32.439 --> 12:33.732
What the hell is this?

12:33.816 --> 12:36.735
Why is everyone gettin' all emotional
without me, huh?

12:36.819 --> 12:38.612
Today is supposed to be my day!

12:38.696 --> 12:41.198
You're not considered
the star of the show, you idiot.

12:41.282 --> 12:42.283
The bride is.

12:42.366 --> 12:43.951
You're more like an extra.

12:44.034 --> 12:46.620
- Okay, but I'm still in the show.
- [laughter]

12:46.704 --> 12:49.707
[Chifuyu] Pah-chin took over
his family's business and got rich.

12:49.790 --> 12:52.084
Apparently,
the bride is a childhood friend.

12:53.002 --> 12:56.380
[Ken] Peh-yan's still by Pah-chin's side,
closer than ever.

12:56.463 --> 12:58.924
[Chifuyu] Mitsuya just started out
as a fashion designer,

12:59.008 --> 13:00.467
but he's already making waves.

13:00.551 --> 13:03.721
He even won an award at a big competition.

13:03.804 --> 13:04.805
Amazing.

13:04.888 --> 13:07.933
[Chifuyu] And get this.
Hakkai's a top model now.

13:08.017 --> 13:10.519
- He gets flown out and works overseas.
- [Takemichi] Whoa!

13:10.602 --> 13:14.231
Hey, Taka, hurry up and get on my level
so we can work together.

13:14.315 --> 13:16.150
Your head is getting too big.

13:16.233 --> 13:18.986
[Chifuyu] Yuzuha keeps Hakkai in check
as his manager.

13:19.069 --> 13:22.865
The Kawata brothers traded guns for knives
and run a ramen shop now.

13:22.948 --> 13:25.826
- Really?
- You should come by and try it sometime.

13:25.909 --> 13:28.245
The recipes we've created are killer.

13:28.329 --> 13:30.414
[Ken] And of course,
the shop's name is "Twin Devils."

13:30.497 --> 13:32.166
Wow!

13:32.249 --> 13:34.835
And Kazutora, he's been working
at Chifuyu's shop.

13:34.918 --> 13:36.795
What the hell are you looking at?

13:36.879 --> 13:38.380
You own a shop too?

13:38.464 --> 13:40.507
Well, yeah, but not what you think.

13:40.591 --> 13:42.676
- He runs a pet shop.
- [Takemichi] What?

13:42.760 --> 13:44.970
It's been his dream, right, Matsuno?

13:45.054 --> 13:47.514
We're still pretty small,
but I know we'll get there.

13:48.015 --> 13:49.224
[Takemichi] That's awesome.

13:49.808 --> 13:52.394
- Congrats, Chifuyu.
- [Chifuyu] Thanks.

13:52.478 --> 13:55.856
By the way. Did you order the carburetor
for Takemitchy's bike?

13:55.939 --> 13:58.192
Yeah, it should get here tomorrow.

13:58.275 --> 13:59.777
What? My bike?

13:59.860 --> 14:02.654
Who do you think took care of your bike
for the past 12 years?

14:02.738 --> 14:06.116
Draken partnered up with Inupi,
and they opened up a bike shop together.

14:07.451 --> 14:10.079
<i>Wow. Everyone's doing so well.</i>

14:11.038 --> 14:12.039
[Naoto] Takemichi.

14:13.499 --> 14:14.792
[gasps]

14:14.875 --> 14:16.627
Good to see that you're finally back.

14:19.254 --> 14:21.423
I never doubted you for a second.

14:23.467 --> 14:25.469
Naoto!

14:25.552 --> 14:29.223
You're alive!
Thank God you're actually alive!

14:29.306 --> 14:32.392
Well, of course.
Did you forget that I'm the trigger?

14:32.476 --> 14:34.728
If I was dead,
you wouldn't have made it back here.

14:34.812 --> 14:36.730
Yeah, I know that, but still...

14:36.814 --> 14:37.981
- [sobbing]
- You did it.

14:38.649 --> 14:40.400
Mission accomplished.

14:42.569 --> 14:44.530
This is a future where my sister is alive.

14:47.116 --> 14:48.117
[Takemichi] <i>That's right.</i>

14:49.535 --> 14:51.453
<i>This is the best future by far.</i>

14:52.162 --> 14:53.413
You don't have to worry.

14:54.331 --> 14:56.750
I promise that we until meet again,

14:56.834 --> 15:00.629
I'll protect everyone in Toman,
and I'll keep Hina safe too.

15:00.712 --> 15:04.216
<i>You kept everyone safe,
just like you promised.</i>

15:04.967 --> 15:06.218
<i>Thank you, Mikey.</i>

15:08.846 --> 15:09.972
- Hey, guys?
- Hmm?

15:10.055 --> 15:11.932
Why haven't I seen Mikey yet?

15:14.351 --> 15:15.394
[both chuckle]

15:20.107 --> 15:24.027
Wow! Can you believe that Mikey's
running a business overseas?

15:24.111 --> 15:25.946
He's really doing big things.

15:26.029 --> 15:29.199
They said he works in food,
but I wonder what exactly.

15:29.283 --> 15:30.784
Maybe like a taiyaki chain.

15:30.868 --> 15:32.703
If it is, I bet it's good.

15:32.786 --> 15:35.914
Being too busy to come just proves
that things are going well for him.

15:35.998 --> 15:37.958
Still a bummer, but I get it.

15:38.041 --> 15:41.044
You know,
it's been pretty busy for us too.

15:41.128 --> 15:43.672
Once we have more time,
we have a lot of things to talk about.

15:43.755 --> 15:45.257
Right.

15:45.340 --> 15:47.259
Uh, what do you mean by that?

15:47.342 --> 15:51.763
I mean, this is probably the busiest
the two of us have ever been.

15:51.847 --> 15:52.848
Huh?

15:52.931 --> 15:54.349
Our wedding is in June.

15:54.433 --> 15:57.311
It'll only be three more months
until we get married.

15:57.394 --> 15:58.854
What?

15:58.937 --> 16:01.440
Twelve years felt like forever.

16:01.523 --> 16:03.025
[sighs] Hina.

16:03.108 --> 16:06.612
You've been carrying the weight
of other people's lives for so long,

16:06.695 --> 16:08.488
you deserve to be selfish now.

16:10.324 --> 16:12.201
So, let's make up for it

16:12.284 --> 16:14.703
by living a life full of happiness.

16:19.374 --> 16:21.627
I hope you're ready
for how busy it's gonna get.

16:21.710 --> 16:25.214
We've booked the venue, and we're
already getting close to our budget.

16:25.297 --> 16:26.965
Not to mention
my dress isn't even ready yet.

16:27.049 --> 16:28.550
[whimpers]

16:28.634 --> 16:31.094
<i>I don't know how much happier I can get.</i>

16:32.346 --> 16:34.640
[Takashi] You're a lucky guy, Takemitchy.

16:35.390 --> 16:38.101
Hina haggled so hard with me,
I couldn't get a word in.

16:38.185 --> 16:40.729
So, is this, like, your workshop?

16:41.230 --> 16:43.440
An acquaintance of mine
actually owns the building.

16:43.523 --> 16:45.651
I just rent the attic 'cause it's cheap.

16:47.402 --> 16:48.904
Is that what I think it is?

16:48.987 --> 16:51.365
Is that the wedding dress
that Hina ordered?

16:51.448 --> 16:52.574
Huh?

16:52.658 --> 16:54.326
Yeah, it is. Like it?

16:54.409 --> 16:57.412
- Like it? I love it! It's beautiful.
- [door opens]

16:57.496 --> 17:00.582
Taka, we got what you asked for.

17:00.666 --> 17:02.251
[Takashi] That took a while.

17:02.334 --> 17:05.128
We got mobbed by some fans
as we were leaving,

17:05.212 --> 17:07.256
and this guy froze up again, as always.

17:08.799 --> 17:10.175
Very nice.

17:10.259 --> 17:13.512
- What's this for?
- It's for your tuxedo, Takemitchy.

17:13.595 --> 17:16.265
Stay still. This is a delicate process.

17:16.348 --> 17:17.724
Okay, got it.

17:17.808 --> 17:20.310
Taka's always serious
when it comes to his fittings.

17:20.394 --> 17:22.646
This is where the magic happens, you know?

17:22.729 --> 17:24.940
- Uh... right.
- Wow.

17:25.023 --> 17:27.192
His face is so handsome
when he's all serious.

17:27.276 --> 17:29.236
Shut up, Hakkai. I'm trying to focus.

17:29.319 --> 17:31.947
I'm really proud of how far
you've come, Mitsuya.

17:32.030 --> 17:34.950
You just went independent, and you've
already gotten all these orders.

17:35.033 --> 17:37.411
Yeah, but the work I've been doing
is grunt work.

17:37.494 --> 17:38.996
Arms up.

17:39.621 --> 17:42.082
Oh, right. You fly back to France today.

17:42.165 --> 17:44.501
Go by Twin Devils.
The Ramen's actually good.

17:44.585 --> 17:47.337
I don't really want to eat ramen
made by those psychos.

17:47.421 --> 17:50.924
And I'd rather swing by Chifuyu's place
to see his doggies one more time.

17:51.800 --> 17:55.053
I think I'll stop by Draken's shop
and get him to rev a bike for me.

17:55.721 --> 17:59.433
That always brings back good memories.
Simpler times.

17:59.516 --> 18:00.767
Hmm.

18:00.851 --> 18:02.102
It's wild.

18:02.185 --> 18:05.689
The last thing I tailored for you
was your Toman uniform.

18:05.772 --> 18:07.899
Yeah, I guess it was.

18:07.983 --> 18:10.611
[laughs]
Some things never change, do they?

18:10.694 --> 18:11.820
[laughing]

18:13.614 --> 18:14.823
[Takemichi] <i>It's nice to see that</i>

18:14.906 --> 18:17.367
<i>everyone's still the same
as they were back then.</i>

18:18.410 --> 18:20.162
Have a good day, sir!

18:21.747 --> 18:24.875
I'm still working in the same video store!

18:24.958 --> 18:26.793
Please put DVDs back on the shelf

18:26.877 --> 18:29.630
a soon as they get returned to us,
Mr. Hanagaki.

18:29.713 --> 18:31.840
Right. Sorry.

18:35.135 --> 18:37.846
This place is as filthy as I remember.

18:40.557 --> 18:43.060
<i>But now, I'm happy.</i>

18:44.394 --> 18:46.063
A FEW DAYS LATER

18:46.146 --> 18:49.524
<i>And now an update on the situation
involving the "Bonten" organization.</i>

18:49.608 --> 18:53.111
<i>- This conflict has...</i>
- [Takemichi] Seriously? That's insane.

18:53.195 --> 18:55.614
Well, I guess gangs like Toman
are still around.

18:55.697 --> 18:59.368
<i>...which we believe could help expose
who the core members are.</i>

19:05.207 --> 19:06.875
[Takemichi] <i>That tattoo...</i>

19:08.418 --> 19:09.795
RAMEN - TWIN DEVILS
RAMEN WHITE

19:09.878 --> 19:13.924
<i>Where have I seen that design before?
I can't place my finger on it.</i>

19:14.007 --> 19:16.385
Hey, did you hear anything I just said?

19:16.468 --> 19:19.638
Of course. You were talking
about the wedding dress, right?

19:19.721 --> 19:20.972
Yeah, you're gonna look amazing.

19:21.056 --> 19:23.225
I was talking about the wedding rehearsal!

19:23.308 --> 19:24.768
You need to stop zoning out!

19:25.727 --> 19:26.812
[Souya] Order up.

19:26.895 --> 19:29.940
Wow, it looks great!
So which one is which?

19:30.023 --> 19:34.152
We call the white tonkotsu "Smiley,"
and the black tonkotsu is named "Angry."

19:34.236 --> 19:38.365
The "Angry" is my go-to. Despite the name,
it's got nice subtle flavors.

19:40.158 --> 19:41.493
[slurping]

19:42.494 --> 19:43.495
Spicy!

19:43.578 --> 19:45.789
"Smiley" looks mild,
but it's got a real kick!

19:45.872 --> 19:48.208
Hmm? That photo...

19:48.792 --> 19:50.627
FIRST GENERATION
TOKYO MANJI

19:50.711 --> 19:53.505
[Souya] Oh. That's a commemorative photo
from when Toman disbanded.

19:53.588 --> 19:56.216
[Nahoya] That was the day
I left my whole youth behind.

19:56.299 --> 19:59.970
March 8th, 12 years ago.
I'll never forget it.

20:00.053 --> 20:02.639
All of us should get together
and catch up soon.

20:03.181 --> 20:05.142
It sounds like Mikey's
been doing well for himself.

20:05.225 --> 20:08.353
- Huh? Is that so?
- Well, we wouldn't know.

20:08.437 --> 20:12.065
What? You guys don't meet up with him
when he's back in Japan?

20:12.149 --> 20:14.401
He's running a restaurant overseas, right?

20:14.484 --> 20:16.528
He does?
That's the first I've heard of it.

20:16.611 --> 20:19.364
Huh?
But that's what Draken and Chifuyu said.

20:19.448 --> 20:22.075
I hear ya.
But did they actually see Mikey?

20:22.159 --> 20:25.495
- What?
- We haven't seen Mikey in over ten years.

20:25.579 --> 20:27.289
It's been that long?

20:27.372 --> 20:29.624
Honestly,
I don't think anyone's seen Mikey.

20:30.709 --> 20:33.462
<i>What the heck? What's going on?</i>

20:33.545 --> 20:35.547
- [metallic tinkling]
- [gasps]

20:37.507 --> 20:39.134
Is something wrong?

20:39.217 --> 20:40.510
[tinkling]

20:43.013 --> 20:44.222
[Takemichi] <i>It just hit me.</i>

20:45.307 --> 20:46.641
<i>That design...</i>

20:47.225 --> 20:49.895
<i>is the same one
on Izana Kurokawa's earring!</i>

20:50.479 --> 20:53.607
- Thanks for the food!
- [Hina] Wait! Takemichi?

20:53.690 --> 20:54.858
[panting]

20:56.401 --> 20:58.028
Mikey's overseas.

20:58.111 --> 21:00.572
He got into the food business
and opened up a restaurant.

21:00.655 --> 21:02.699
He's been doing really well over there.

21:02.783 --> 21:06.536
[Takemichi] <i>I don't know why,
but I've got a bad feeling about this!</i>

21:07.788 --> 21:09.122
Draken!

21:09.206 --> 21:12.709
Takemitchy?
Why do you look like you've seen a ghost?

21:12.793 --> 21:14.294
Why did you lie to me, Draken?

21:15.337 --> 21:17.339
The whole thing
about Mikey being overseas...

21:17.422 --> 21:18.840
It's a lie, isn't it?

21:21.092 --> 21:24.679
Smiley and the others said
they haven't seen him in over ten years.

21:25.263 --> 21:27.724
And Mitsuya said
he hasn't seen him either.

21:28.433 --> 21:31.186
And today, as I was watching the news,

21:31.269 --> 21:34.105
I saw someone
who almost looked like Izana Kurokawa.

21:35.148 --> 21:37.943
What if Izana survived that last fight?

21:38.652 --> 21:40.070
What if he's still breathing?

21:40.946 --> 21:42.531
What if he went after Mikey?

21:42.614 --> 21:43.615
BIKER GANG

21:43.698 --> 21:47.077
<i>Izana Kurokawa resented Mikey
until his last breath,</i>

21:47.577 --> 21:50.747
even though Mikey forgave him
for killing Emma.

21:51.790 --> 21:52.958
Don't tell me...

21:53.542 --> 21:54.918
Mikey was killed by Izana?

21:56.711 --> 21:59.506
<i>And here I thought
this was the best future...</i>

22:00.757 --> 22:02.551
Now please tell me the truth.

22:03.593 --> 22:06.429
What really happened to Mikey?
Is he alive?

22:11.059 --> 22:13.395
[♪ theme music playing]

23:41.024 --> 23:42.025
FAIRY TALE REVENGERS
PETIT

23:42.108 --> 23:43.526
<i>- Fairy Tale Revengers.
- Fairy Tale Revengers.</i>

23:43.610 --> 23:45.820
Hey! Why hasn't my horn grown back yet?

23:45.904 --> 23:48.281
Well, it looks like it snapped off
at the base.

23:48.365 --> 23:50.367
That's gonna take a while to grow back.

23:50.450 --> 23:53.870
[growls]
I'm going to kill that peach bastard.

23:53.954 --> 23:56.998
Hey! Anyone got something
we can use as a horn for now?

23:58.541 --> 23:59.542
ROCK

23:59.626 --> 24:01.127
Way too small. Try again!

24:01.211 --> 24:02.212
FLOWER

24:02.295 --> 24:04.381
What <i>oni</i> wears flowers? Try again!

24:04.464 --> 24:05.966
BUNNY EARS

24:06.049 --> 24:07.384
Do you wanna die?

24:07.467 --> 24:08.468
Forget it.

24:08.551 --> 24:11.221
I'll just break off my horn
and give it to the boss.

24:12.305 --> 24:14.808
If you do that, you'll be hurt too.

24:14.891 --> 24:17.560
But I can't just leave you without a horn.

24:17.644 --> 24:19.646
- I don't need yours.
- You sure?

24:19.729 --> 24:22.399
I'll just rip off a horn
from that bunny-eared dumbass.

24:22.482 --> 24:24.109
[gulping]

24:24.776 --> 24:25.777
Izana!

24:25.860 --> 24:26.945
TO BE CONTINUED
